well our trip to the grocery store has  certainly changed dramatically in the  last year  an entrepreneur created something out of  necessity to make us all feel a little  bit safer while we're grocery shopping  and she believes that it is still going  to be a necessity long after covid is  gone  kirsten joyce has the story denise when  the pandemic hit  mom and entrepreneur andy barnes rubin  was scared to go to the grocery store  and when she did a little research about  just how dirty grocery carts were  it only confirmed her worst fears  grocery carts are  more disgusting and have just as much  bacteria as a public toilet  and that that freaked me out  and that's research from the university  of arizona's department of environmental  science  well andy wanted to create a  one-size-fits-all liner that covers the  entire grocery cart including the handle  for carts as large as say costco and as  small as trader joe's  within a few months she had a prototype  a patent she got it manufactured and  launched it nationwide in august  right now she offers a recyclable  shopping cart liner  you get a package of 10 sells for about  19.99  and very soon she'll be offering another  option  i discovered that a lot of people wanted  something that you could just throw in  the washing machine so  within about two weeks we will be  getting our cart safe  washable liners so that's really  exciting because i know  you know there's people that don't like  the recycled plastic but they're gonna  love this so i wanted to make sure that  whatever people were more comfortable  with that they had the options  she says even when the coronavirus goes  away we still got to battle the germs  and dirt and she says this device will  keep her family  safe and yours andy is currently  pursuing a good housekeeping seal of  approval  for the product
 

